From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] conhost: true colours in a Terminal tab

Claude Code draws in true colour (SGR 38;2 / 48;2): its mascot, its
syntax colours, its diff's red and green rows. The console kept each cell
as one of the 16 console colours and sent the tab that, so it "looked off"
(David 2026-10-01) -- the mascot grey, the diff's rows gone, the colours
wrong. Each cell now keeps its true colours beside its attribute (the
nearest of the 16 stays there for programs that read the cells back), set
by SGR 38;2 / 48;2 / 38;5 (16-255), cleared by the plain colours, 39, 49, 0
and by the console API's attribute writes, and moved, scrolled, filled,
resized and saved with the alternate screen as the cells are. The tab
(sg-terminal, a pseudo console's terminal) gets them as 38;2 / 48;2.

A line feed that scrolls a terminal fills the new line with the background
in effect; the console's new lines are blank, so the background is made
plain before the console sends a line feed -- a row's colour ran on into
the next row.

Test: test/claudecon-gate.sh (mutants SG_MUTANT_NO_TRUECOLOR,
SG_MUTANT_LF_KEEPS_BG).
